1
00:00:10,790 --> 00:00:17,152
A vehicle is not a row in a list. It
is a thing with a history and a cost.

2
00:00:17,605 --> 00:00:23,596
Who has it now is the easy half, and it
is on the record where anybody can see it.

3
00:00:24,048 --> 00:00:31,107
Who had it before is the half that
matters, kept as periods rather than overwritten.

4
00:00:31,557 --> 00:00:37,734
Which is what lets the costs sit
under the right name, period by period.

5
00:00:38,185 --> 00:00:44,222
Handing it over says what it will do
before you agree to it, rather than after.

6
00:00:44,674 --> 00:00:50,724
Correct a handover date later and the
whole ledger re-attributes itself, because

7
00:00:50,724 --> 00:00:53,219
nothing wrote a name onto a cost.

8
00:00:53,671 --> 00:00:57,247
Next: turning finished
work into an invoice.

